    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Consider implementing sampling strategies to manage data volume without losing critical information. Always log 100% of errors, slow requests (P95+), and requests with negative user feedback. For normal successful requests, implement stratified sampling that maintains representative coverage across different dimensions. Sample 10% of requests per model version, per use case, and per user cohort. This ensures you have statistical coverage while reducing storage costs. Some teams implement dynamic sampling that increases sample rates when quality metrics start degrading, giving you higher resolution data exactly when you need it most for investigation."
